# Short article.

title "Why I rewrote my blog in EZHTML"
subtitle "Lessons from a weekend migration"

text "I have written four blogs in five years. Each one taught me the same lesson: most of the friction comes from the markup, not the words."

space

text "EZHTML removes closing tags, pretty-prints itself, and gives me warnings on accessibility issues. I shipped the new site in an afternoon."

quote "The fastest way to ship is to write less." "me, just now"

text "Here is the full diff."

code "git diff --stat old-blog new-blog" "git"

text "Forty-two lines of HTML became six lines of EZHTML. The mental cost dropped even more."
